### Page 4 of 11

```text
Final Plat | UDC-19-00743
3
EXECUTIVE SUMMARY:

This plat proposes dividing one large parcel into 17 parcels. The proposal includes 8 lots for duplex
development, 6 lots for townhome development, one parcel for detention, one parcel for open space, and
one parcel for the existing church. The property is currently within City limits and zoned MR Medium-
density Residential.

The layout of the Final Plat is substantially similar to the layout of the approved Preliminary Plat. The
Final Plat has appropriately addressed the conditions placed on the Preliminary Plat approval. Jackson
Street was designated as a collector street, but was not functioning as a collector (due to the low traffic
counts and limited potential for future development to add traffic). The Metropolitan Planning
Organization Policy Committee met on December 19, 2019, and officially changed Jackson Street’s
classification to a local street.

The transportation network in this area of the community is previously developed, and there is limited
opportunity for this plat to contribute to the street network.

Due to meeting the review criteria set forth in Section 2.1.3.d of the Cheyenne Unified
Development Code, staff recommends the Planning Commission approve this final plat.
```

