### Page 7 of 11

```text
Final Plat | UDC-19-00743
6

FINAL PLAT DATA:  In reviewing, providing comments, and making recommendations and decisions on
a proposed final plat, the Staff, Planning Commission and City Council shall use the following 3 criteria, as
found in Section 2.1.3.d:

1. CONFORMANCE WITH PRELIMINARY PLAT - The layout and design of the final plat is in substantial
compliance with the approved preliminary plat considering the number of lots or parcels, street and block
layout, and access, and any deviations in the final plat brings the application in further compliance with
the Comprehensive Plan.

The final plat as submitted is substantially similar to the layout shown in the approved preliminary
plat. The ownership parcel containing the existing church has been included within the plat boundary.
A drainage easement not shown on the preliminary plat has been added to the final plat. Lots,
blocks, and easements are all aligned according to the approved preliminary plat.

Lots 1-6 are proposed as townhome lots (AD1). Lots 8-9 and 11-16 are proposed as duplex lots
(SD3). Lot 7 is designated for open space. Lot 10 is designated for open space and drainage. Lot 17
contains the existing church.

Alliance Addition, 4th Filing Final Plat Map.
```

### Page 8 of 11

```text
Final Plat | UDC-19-00743
7

2. CONDITIONS - The application meets any conditions or modifications of the approved preliminary plat.

The following conditions were placed on the Preliminary Plat:
1. The final plat and associated submittal documents shall include the entirety of the parent
tract, including the church. The church lot shall be platted as an individual lot.
2. Block(s) shall be numbered.
3. For final plat submittal, dedicate 10’ of additional right-of-way to the north side of Jackson
Street, and provide an alley or access easement to allow rear access to all parcels fronting
Jackson Street – unless Jackson Street has been reclassified as a local street (or substantial
progress has been made to reclassify Jackson Street by the appropriate agencies).
The Final Plat map submitted fulfills conditions 1 and 2. The Metropolitan Planning Organization
Policy Committee met on December 19, 2019, and officially changed Jackson Street’s classification to
local street. This reclassification by the policy committee effectively fulfills condition number 3.

3. SUBDIVISION STANDARDS - The application meets the purposes, intent, and applicable standards of
Article 4.

Transportation Network:
This plat is part of a block which has a perimeter of about 3,500’. The standard for maximum
perimeter for newly developing residential areas is 2,200’. However, due to the surrounding
development patterns, there is little opportunity for this plat to create a meaningful break in the
existing block. Due to the previous development patterns, and as this plat is under 10 acres,
Staff’s judgement is that the plat qualifies for the infill exception from maximum block sizes (UDC
4.3.3.c.6).

Community Facility Fees:
This land was previously platted in 1981 as Alliance Addition. The City charged plat fees at the
rate of $400 per acre in 1980’s, and the land contained within this replat is presumed to have
paid the appropriate plat fees with the original plat; therefore $2,240 will be credited toward this
proposed plat’s fees. This plat proposes platting the subject property for residential development.
The Residential enhancement fee is $400 per unit, and 14 residential lots are proposed.
For fees based on acreage, the area of the plat is pro-rated to the nearest tenth of an acre.
There are approximately 5.6 acres of land contained within the plat boundary.
The required fees for the 5.6 acres of non-exempt land in this plat are as follows:
Land Acquisition Fee

$1,960 ($350 per acre)
Infrastructure Fee

$1,960 ($350 per acre)
Credit for plat fees previously paid
-$2,240
Total Land Acquisition & Infrastructure Fees:  $1,680.00
Per UDC Section 4.2.5, Table 4-2, the Land Acquisition & Infrastructure fee are payable at
the time of the signing of the final plat.

Projected Residential Enhancement Fee
$5,600 ($400 per unit)
Per UDC Section 4.2.5, Table 4-2, Enhancement Fees are payable at the issuance of a
building permit for each structure.
```

### Page 9 of 11

```text
Final Plat | UDC-19-00743
8
Open Space:
During the plat process, this property is not required to provide open space. Residential open
space is not required at time of platting on infill development of less than 10 acres, as long as
alternative open space options are available (UDC 4.4.3.b.3). The applicant has indicated the
intent to meet the requirements of on-site open space found in Article 6 (UDC 6.6.3.a.2), by
providing yards and patios. The applicant has also indicated the church property may effectively
serve as open space available to these residents. The plat also includes a detention pond parcel
and an open space parcel to provide a frontage for the proposed townhome lots 2, 4, and 6.

Required Improvements:
This division can provide all required utilities to the properties within this development.

REVIEW

REVIEWING AGENCIES WITH COMMENTS:
-
Development (Susana Montana and Seth Lloyd)
o
(FYI) The “1” in “Block 1” gets lost in the lower lot, please make it more prominent.
o
(FYI) The transportation worksheet may need to include the traffic or trip counts for the
church.
o
(FYI) All conditions appear fulfilled with final plat submittal.
o
(FYI) Final Plat layout is substantially similar to Preliminary Plat layout.
-
Laramie County Assessor (Clarice Blanton)
o
(FYI) Note 11 states Lot 7 is granted to Owners of Lots 2, 4 and 6. Will the interest be
on an equal undivided basis? Any document which transfers interest of Lots 2, 4 and 6
should also transfer the interest in Lot 7.
-
Laramie County School District #1 (Chris Hout)
o
(FYI) This This development site falls within the East Triad -- student’s home attendance
boundaries are East High School, Carey Junior High School and Meadowlark (5-6) and
Buffalo Ridge (K-4) Elementary Schools. The current attendance for these schools is as
follows:
▪
Buffalo Ridge (grades K-4) -- below capacity, some space available most grades.
▪
Meadowlark Elementary (grades 5-6) -- at or near capacity, limited space may be
available both grades
▪
Carey Junior High -- slightly below capacity with some space available in both
grades.
▪
East High -- Near or at capacity, limited to no space available all grades.
-
Suncor (Dillon Ohrt)
o
(FYI) Suncor and applicant have entered into an agreement regarding development on
Suncor’s easement. Suncor has no objections to the project.
All other reviewing agencies did not provide comments.

OTHER COMMENTS RECEIVED:
-
None

